\description{
Long tidy tibble of equal-weight rollup scores, one row per
\strong{unit x year x ctf_type x node}, where a node is a real taxonomy tier
(\code{subcluster} / \code{sub_subcluster} / \code{cluster} / \code{overall}). Built by
\code{\link[=roll_up_scores]{roll_up_scores()}} from the country rows of \code{cgjr_ctf}, with region /
income-group rows appended by \code{\link[=aggregate_to_groups]{aggregate_to_groups()}}.

\strong{Rollup (order ii, within country).} A leaf's score is the mean of its
indicators' \code{ctf} values; a branching subcluster's score (Public Financial
Management only) is the mean of its \code{sub_subcluster} scores; a cluster's
score is the mean of its subclusters' scores; \code{overall} is the mean of the
cluster scores. \code{NA} is lenient (\code{na.rm = TRUE}) at every stage; all
children missing yields \code{NA} (never \code{NaN}). The finest grain is scaffolded
against every \code{cgjr_taxonomy} leaf first, so a leaf with zero eligible
indicators for a \code{ctf_type} still gets a row (\code{score = NA}, \code{n_inputs = 0})
rather than silently vanishing.

\strong{There is no stored "is this the finest grain" flag.} Every plain
subcluster reports once, at \code{node_level == "subcluster"}, and \emph{is} the
finest grain for its branch; only Public Financial Management also carries
\code{node_level == "sub_subcluster"} rows one level finer. To select every
finest-grain node regardless of depth:

